  "behavior": [
    "i8 reads through the shared UTF-8 decoder with unsigned byte bits, matching native reinterpretation. All 256 leading bytes and padded malformed sequences are probed.",
    "Signed destinations reuse the encoder and preserve untouched buffer tails for valid, surrogate and out-of-range symbols.",
    "UtfUnit now requires to_bits instead of Into<u32>; signed-byte conversions preserve storage bits. Existing unsigned unit and UTF string conversion paths are regression-tested.",
    "Initial validation caught a redundant u32 cast and a generic oracle formatter still requiring Into<u32>. Both were corrected before the frozen full validation."
  ],
  "remaining_gaps": [
    "ChangeBufferHere writable aliases remain unavailable on shared input slices.",
    "Input slices synthesize zero padding; padding addresses are not dereferenceable storage. Null increment remains a Rust panic instead of undefined native behavior.",
    "Signed16/32 behavior has subsequent scoped evidence in utf-signed-wide-contracts.json. Arbitrary size-dispatched native types and platform-specific wchar_t ABI configurations remain unproven.",
    "The checked destination slice API returns a buffer-size error where native output would overrun; invalid pointer domains are excluded."
  ]
}
